// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 296: Contiguous address space in pss_top (page 402)
component pss_top {
   import addr_reg_pkg::*;
my_ip_c ip;
contiguous_addr_space_c<> sys_mem;
exec init_up {
          // Add regions to space here
          addr_region_s<> r1;
          r1.size = 0x40000000; // 1 GB
          (void)sys_mem.add_region(r1);
          addr_region_s<> mmio;
          mmio.size = 4096;
          (void)sys_mem.add_nonallocatable_region(mmio);
}
}

Syntax 123—Transparent address space component
24.7.1.5 Other address spaces
Other kinds of address spaces, with different assumptions on allocations and generic operations, are
possible. These may be represented as derived types of the corresponding base space/region/claim types. An
example could be a space representing a routing table in a network router. PSS does not attempt to
standardize these.
24.7.2 Address space traits
An address space trait is a PSS struct. A trait struct describes properties of a contiguous address space and
its regions. empty_addr_trait_s is defined as an empty trait struct that is used as the default trait type
for address spaces, regions and claims.
